            <div xml:id="d985">

                <pb facs="0766" n="690" xml:id="pg690"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.48/3080</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Mr.
                            Arredondo, representing American
                        interests in Mexico</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-05-13T14:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 13, 1916, 2 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>330. See Department’s 286, March 20, and hand copy thereof to Rodgers, for his
                    information. Telegraph number Americans, especially women and children, that
                    have followed advice in said instruction, and again advise Americans, whose
                    presence in Mexico City is not absolutely essential for business reasons, to
                    return to this country.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
